Years ago, long before I even knew about the existence of the net, a
friend gave me a copy of Hack 1.0.1E for the PC.  I played it for a
while and enjoyed it a lot.
As time went on, I became a shareware author, and one day decided to
look through the .DOC file again to see if hack was shareware.  It
was, so I sent $35 to Don Kneller, and soon afterwards I received in
the mail a diskette with the source and executable for PC Hack 3.0
About a year later, another friend gave me nethack 1.4.  So, once
again, I checked the .DOC file, and sent some money to the address
noted, as well as a request for the latest version.
It's been over a year, and so far no response, and my check was never
cashed.  It's not that important now, I can download nethack 3.0 pl8
when it appears in comp.sources.games, but my question is:
Is nethack sharware?  Who accepts registration fees?  And why was mine
ignored for so long?

